{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00626",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.11,
      "end_seconds": 10.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.58,
      "text": "Good morning. I've kept a log since our last appointment, if that's useful. It's on my phone. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.72,
      "end_seconds": 20.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "Brilliant, I'll look at it in a minute. Headlines first. How are you doing? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.74,
      "end_seconds": 34.05,
      "duration_seconds": 12.31,
      "text": "Mixed. The washing is still there. I wash my hands around thirty times a day, down from about fifty in the autumn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.06,
      "end_seconds": 42.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.55,
      "text": "Thirty is still a lot. Walk me through what a typical day looks like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.7,
      "end_seconds": 58.03,
      "duration_seconds": 13.33,
      "text": "Every time I touch a door handle, a keyboard, anything from outside, I feel contaminated, and I can't settle until I've washed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.58,
      "end_seconds": 66.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "Is the anxious feeling worse when you try not to wash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.15,
      "end_seconds": 78.41,
      "duration_seconds": 11.26,
      "text": "Much worse. I feel anxious when I can't wash, like something terrible is about to happen. It builds until I give in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.35,
      "end_seconds": 83.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "And your hands, how are they?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.07,
      "end_seconds": 91.9,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "Sore. They crack and bleed in the winter. I've been using more cream."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.25,
      "end_seconds": 100.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Let's go through the tablets. What are you on right now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.24,
      "end_seconds": 121.6,
      "duration_seconds": 20.36,
      "text": "Fluoxetine, 40 mg once a day in the morning. Then a small white tablet that the clinic added in the summer, I couldn't tell you the name, only that it's round with a line through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.42,
      "end_seconds": 133.63,
      "duration_seconds": 11.21,
      "text": "Okay, I'll look it up on your record, but for now I'll note that you can't name it. And the third?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.49,
      "end_seconds": 140.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "Melatonin, 2 mg at night, when my mind won't switch off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.33,
      "end_seconds": 146.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Good. Any thoughts of harming yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.68,
      "end_seconds": 156.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "No. None at all. It's the opposite, I'm frightened of germs, not of dying."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.57,
      "end_seconds": 162.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Thank you for being direct. What's your background, health-wise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.51,
      "end_seconds": 172.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "OCD, diagnosed six years ago. And I've had eczema since I was little."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.8,
      "end_seconds": 177.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Do you work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.78,
      "end_seconds": 187.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.94,
      "text": "Yes, I work as a librarian. Handling books is fine, it's the returns bin I dread."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.69,
      "end_seconds": 215.42,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "Pulse 70, blood pressure 122 over 76, temperature 36.4, oxygen 99 percent. And weight 61 kilos, which matches last time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.82,
      "end_seconds": 221.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "I've lost nothing, then. Good. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.94,
      "end_seconds": 227.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Let me see your hands. Palms up. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.06,
      "end_seconds": 231.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "They're not pretty. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.81,
      "end_seconds": 250.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Dry, cracked skin across both knuckles, with a split here on the right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.69,
      "end_seconds": 255.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "It stings in the shower. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.93,
      "end_seconds": 266.18,
      "duration_seconds": 9.25,
      "text": "I can't rule out the eczema flaring on top of the washing, which would explain some of the soreness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.53,
      "end_seconds": 274.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.06,
      "text": "Could the washing itself be making the eczema worse? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.03,
      "end_seconds": 289.51,
      "duration_seconds": 12.48,
      "text": "Very likely. It's a loop, the more you wash, the more the skin breaks. That's why I want to push the therapy harder. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.32,
      "end_seconds": 298.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "I'm willing. The exposure exercises are hard but I did four of them last week. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.38,
      "end_seconds": 311.24,
      "duration_seconds": 10.86,
      "text": "That's excellent. Keep going with those, and use a thick emollient straight after each wash rather than waiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.33,
      "end_seconds": 319.58,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "I'll set a reminder. Anything else I should do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.03,
      "end_seconds": 333.54,
      "duration_seconds": 11.51,
      "text": "I'd like to check your blood, a routine blood test, to make sure nothing physical is adding to your anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.47,
      "end_seconds": 337.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Fine. And the next appointment? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.39,
      "end_seconds": 345.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Come back in six weeks, and bring the log again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.04,
      "end_seconds": 350.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Six weeks. Thank you, doctor. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.11,
      "end_seconds": 356.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Well done for keeping the log. ~"
    }
  ]
}
